[D] the gauntlets of power, tinning kit and unicorn horn can all indirectly
[D] affect the same stat, you must choose wisely ...
[D] and with the athame you effectively don't need the tinning kit.

let me explain ... i had improperly focussed on the strength stat.

_for me_, the best use of the tinning kit is to can giants and wraiths
(and other fruitful monsters) in the heat of battle. for this advantage
you've got to carry a _heavy_ tinning kit. since giants often travel in
groups and eating giant corpses is desirable the tinning kit is a strategic
item. also, tins are less filling but otherwise equal to corpses ...

the unicorn horn is effectively restore ability on a stick. once restored,
and by mid-game it is unlikely that you'll want to carry the unicorn horn.
however, it is still a good rustproof weapon (better if it has plusses).

while worn, the gauntlets of power maintain your strength stat at 25
regardless of what happens to your ungloved strength stat.

the athame allows you to take a break in the heat of battle (mostly).
during this break you can eat the corpse that you would have otherwise
canned. if you get satiated you can cast worthless spells or attempt
teleports to burn-off food quickly. if i have an athame i won't carry
a tinning kit (hopefully i can carry other useful magic instead).

this style of play is not for everyone ...
note: i don't carry pick-axes since dwarves and minotaurs deliver, also.
things i find important are being able to force a teleport, telepathy
and a way to use it, poison resistance ...

